00:56:27,514 --> 00:56:31,183
Just don't put yourself
in this type of position.

1051
00:56:31,183 --> 00:56:32,559
What type of position?

1052
00:56:32,559 --> 00:56:37,105
Position of being humiliated.

1053
00:56:45,030 --> 00:56:47,824
sean, would you like
to hear me tell a joke?

1054
00:56:47,824 --> 00:56:50,744
Yeah, sure.

1055
00:56:50,744 --> 00:56:53,830
Knock, knock!

1056
00:56:55,415 --> 00:56:59,294
so, my-my next question is,
when a pilot retires

1057
00:56:59,294 --> 00:57:02,840
uh, Pan Am sends them
a check every single month?

1058
00:57:02,840 --> 00:57:06,719
Uh, yeah, pension program
sends a check and benefits.

1059
00:57:06,719 --> 00:57:08,345
How much is that check for?

1060
00:57:08,345 --> 00:57:10,931
Uh, kid, I'm really not
in the mood for this right now.

1061
00:57:10,931 --> 00:57:12,432
This skywayman's
driving me crazy.

1062
00:57:12,432 --> 00:57:13,851
Who's the skywayman?

1063
00:57:13,851 --> 00:57:15,853
Ah, some nut that's flying
around the country

1064
00:57:15,853 --> 00:57:17,104
posing as a Pan Am pilot.

1065
00:57:17,104 --> 00:57:20,983
There's a column about him
in the paper today.

1066
00:57:25,779 --> 00:57:28,448
I keep telling them
this is not my problem.

1067
00:57:28,448 --> 00:57:30,492
This guy
doesn't even fly Pan Am.

1068
00:57:30,492 --> 00:57:31,827
Flies everybody else.

1069
00:57:31,827 --> 00:57:34,454
Flies United, TWA,
Continental, Eastern...

1070
00:57:34,454 --> 00:57:36,957
The skywayman.

1071
00:57:36,957 --> 00:57:39,293
Newspaper loves this clown.

1072
00:57:39,293 --> 00:57:42,671
They call him
"the James Bond of the sky."

1073
00:57:45,465 --> 00:57:46,550
Did you say...?

1074
00:57:46,550 --> 00:57:48,343
Bond, James Bond.

1075
00:57:57,311 --> 00:58:00,105
Tell me, Joan,
why does he do it?

1076
00:58:00,105 --> 00:58:01,565
He likes to win.

1077
00:58:01,565 --> 00:58:02,608
Come on, come on.

1078
00:58:02,608 --> 00:58:04,110
We'll be landing
in 20 minutes.

1079
00:58:04,110 --> 00:58:06,945
Do you want to play it easy
or the hard way?

1080
00:58:06,945 --> 00:58:08,948
And this isn't a tranquilizer.

1081
00:58:08,948 --> 00:58:12,326
Well, Pussy, you do know a lot
more about planes than guns.

1082
00:58:12,326 --> 00:58:14,620
Hello, Pussy.

1083
00:58:14,620 --> 00:58:16,456
Now, you're sure

1084
00:58:16,456 --> 00:58:17,831
this is the suit, right?

1085
00:58:17,831 --> 00:58:18,999
Positive.

1086
00:58:18,999 --> 00:58:20,834
It's the exact suit he wore
in the movie.

1087
00:58:20,834 --> 00:58:22,836
Okay. I'll take three.

1088
00:58:22,836 --> 00:58:24,505
Certainly, Mr. Fleming.

1089
00:58:24,505 --> 00:58:26,840
Now what you need is
one of those

1090
00:58:26,840 --> 00:58:29,801
little foreign sports cars
that he drives.

1091
00:58:49,196 --> 00:58:53,742
The look of love

1092
00:58:53,742 --> 00:58:57,037
Is in your eyes...

1093
00:58:57,037 --> 00:58:58,038
Hello.

1094
00:58:58,038 --> 00:58:59,373
Hi.

1095
00:58:59,373 --> 00:59:01,835
...The look your heart...

1096
00:59:01,835 --> 00:59:04,670
Haven't I seen you before?

1097
00:59:04,670 --> 00:59:06,713
...Can't disguise...

1098
00:59:06,713 --> 00:59:08,048
Maybe.

1099
00:59:08,048 --> 00:59:11,885
A couple years ago, I was
on the cover of Seventeen.

1100
00:59:11,885 --> 00:59:13,387
Yeah.

1101
00:59:13,387 --> 00:59:14,888
You're that model, right?

1102
00:59:14,888 --> 00:59:16,056
Cheryl.

1103
00:59:16,056 --> 00:59:17,182
Yes.

1104
00:59:17,182 --> 00:59:20,602
The guys used to put
your picture on their lockers.

1105
00:59:20,602 --> 00:59:25,190
Isn't that your silver car
I saw parked out front?

1106
00:59:25,190 --> 00:59:28,569
Yeah. One of them.

1107
00:59:28,569 --> 00:59:31,738
Well, it takes
my breath away...

1108
00:59:31,738 --> 00:59:35,158
so, think I could get
an autograph?

1109
00:59:35,158 --> 00:59:36,994
...I can hardly wait
to hold you

1110
00:59:36,994 --> 00:59:38,579
Feel my arms around you...

1111
00:59:38,579 --> 00:59:40,414
Do you have a pen in your room?

1112
00:59:40,414 --> 00:59:42,165
...How long I have waited...

1113
00:59:56,597 --> 01:00:02,102
You've got the look of love

1114
01:00:02,102 --> 01:00:07,274
It's on your face

1115
01:00:07,274 --> 01:00:16,116
A look that time
can't erase...

1116
01:00:16,116 --> 01:00:17,451
shh.

1117
01:00:17,451 --> 01:00:18,952
...Be mine tonight...

1118
01:00:18,952 --> 01:00:23,832
Man like you can buy
anything he wants.

1119
01:00:23,832 --> 01:00:26,960
...Let this be
just the start

1120
01:00:26,960 --> 01:00:34,134
Of so many nights
like this...

1121
01:00:34,134 --> 01:00:36,970
He buys a deck of cards
at the hotel gift shop.

1122
01:00:36,970 --> 01:00:40,140
...And then seal it
with a kiss...

1123
01:00:40,140 --> 01:00:42,809
Well, you want
to see a card trick?

1124
01:00:42,809 --> 01:00:44,478
...I can hardly wait
to hold you...

1125
01:00:44,478 --> 01:00:46,313
How much did these cards cost?

1126
01:00:46,313 --> 01:00:48,482
...Feel my arms
around you...

1127
01:00:48,482 --> 01:00:50,609
Oh, 55 cents, I think.

1128
01:00:50,609 --> 01:00:53,153
...Waited just
to love you...

1129
01:00:53,153 --> 01:00:59,159
And if they sold me downstairs
at the hotel gift shop...

1130
01:00:59,159 --> 01:01:01,787
how much would you pay?

1131
01:01:01,787 --> 01:01:03,997
I'm sor...

1132
01:01:03,997 --> 01:01:07,709
I'm sorry, how mu...
how much would I pay for what?

1133
01:01:10,337 --> 01:01:13,841
The entire night.

1134
01:01:13,841 --> 01:01:18,637
How much would you pay me
for the entire night?

1135
01:01:22,182 --> 01:01:25,686
Cheryl, I...
I really don't know.

1136
01:01:25,686 --> 01:01:27,020
...I can hardly wait
to hold you...

1137
01:01:27,020 --> 01:01:29,857
Don't be scared.

1138
01:01:29,857 --> 01:01:32,860
...How long I have waited...

1139
01:01:32,860 --> 01:01:35,946
Make me an offer.

1140
01:01:35,946 --> 01:01:39,283
...Now that I have found you

1141
01:01:39,283 --> 01:01:42,870
Don't ever go...

1142
01:01:42,870 --> 01:01:44,955
$300?

1143
01:01:44,955 --> 01:01:46,832
Go fish.

1144
01:01:49,334 --> 01:01:52,880
Uh, $500?

1145
01:01:52,880 --> 01:01:54,715
Go fish.

1146
01:01:55,757 --> 01:01:57,384
$600.

1147
01:01:58,760 --> 01:02:01,180
Go fish.

1148
01:02:03,223 --> 01:02:05,225
$1,000.

1149
01:02:07,394 --> 01:02:08,979
Okay.

1150
01:02:08,979 --> 01:02:13,066
$1,000.

1151
01:02:13,066 --> 01:02:15,903
Okay.

1152
01:02:15,903 --> 01:02:18,363
I'll be right back.

1153
01:02:18,363 --> 01:02:20,365
Wait a second.
Where are you going?

1154
01:02:20,365 --> 01:02:22,576
I'm going downstairs
to cash a check.

1155
01:02:22,576 --> 01:02:26,288
You think this hotel is going
to cash a $1,000 check

1156
01:02:26,288 --> 01:02:27,623
at 3:00am?

1157
01:02:30,667 --> 01:02:32,586
It's a New York savings and Loan
check.

1158
01:02:32,586 --> 01:02:33,754
It's like gold.

1159
01:02:33,754 --> 01:02:34,880
They'll cash it.

1160
01:02:34,880 --> 01:02:37,841
Don't you think they might get
a little suspicious?

1161
01:02:37,841 --> 01:02:38,842
Let me see that.

1162
01:02:38,842 --> 01:02:41,553
It's a cashier's check.

1163
01:02:41,553 --> 01:02:43,263
Endorse it over to me.

1164
01:02:43,263 --> 01:02:45,140
No. I couldn't do that.

1165
01:02:45,140 --> 01:02:47,601
see, this check is for $1,400.

1166
01:02:47,601 --> 01:02:50,145
We agreed upon $1,000.

1167
01:02:50,145 --> 01:02:56,777
Why don't I give you back $400
and you give me that check?

1168
01:02:56,777 --> 01:02:59,446
Even better.

1169
01:03:02,282 --> 01:03:07,120
The look of love

1170
01:03:07,120 --> 01:03:13,085
Is in your eyes...

1171
01:03:30,310 --> 01:03:33,647
Does this belong to anybody?

1172
01:03:41,780 --> 01:03:44,616
Mele Kalikimaka
is the thing to say...

1173
01:03:46,702 --> 01:03:49,496
On a bright
Hawaiian Christmas Day...

1174
01:03:49,496 --> 01:03:51,498
This is Hanratty.
Merry Christmas.

1175
01:03:51,498 --> 01:03:52,466
Hello, Carl.

1176
01:03:52,466 --> 01:03:52,958
Hello.

1177
01:03:54,793 --> 01:03:57,337
...That we send to you,
from the land...

1178
01:03:57,337 --> 01:03:59,339
Barry Allen, secret service.

1179
01:03:59,339 --> 01:04:02,050
I've been trying
to track you down now

1180
01:04:02,050 --> 01:04:04,136
for the last couple of hours.

1181
01:04:04,136 --> 01:04:05,387
What do you want?

1182
01:04:05,387 --> 01:04:08,849
I wanted to apologize
for what happened

1183
01:04:08,849 --> 01:04:10,350
out in Los Angeles.

1184
01:04:10,350 --> 01:04:11,518
Uh-uh, uh-uh.

1185
01:04:11,518 --> 01:04:13,645
No, no,
you don't apologize to me.

1186
01:04:13,645 --> 01:04:16,273
Do you always work
on Christmas Eve, Carl?

1187
01:04:16,273 --> 01:04:17,858
I volunteered

1188
01:04:17,858 --> 01:04:20,861
so men with families
could go home early.

1189
01:04:20,861 --> 01:04:22,988
Looked like you were wearing
a wedding ring

1190
01:04:22,988 --> 01:04:24,072
out in Los Angeles.

1191
01:04:24,072 --> 01:04:25,741
I thought maybe
you had a family.

1192
01:04:25,741 --> 01:04:29,203
No. No family.

1193
01:04:29,203 --> 01:04:31,205
You want to talk to me...

1194
01:04:31,205 --> 01:04:33,166
let's talk face-to-face.

1195
01:04:33,166 --> 01:04:34,625
All right.

1196
01:04:34,625 --> 01:04:38,670
I'm at my suite at the
stuyvesant Arms, room 3113.

1197
01:04:38,670 --> 01:04:42,841
In the morning, I leave
for Las Vegas for the weekend.

1198
01:04:42,841 --> 01:04:46,887
You think you're going
to get me again?

1199
01:04:46,887 --> 01:04:48,680
You're not going to Vegas.

1200
01:04:48,680 --> 01:04:50,682
You're not
in the stuyvesant Arms.

1201
01:04:50,682 --> 01:04:52,351
You'd love for me

1202
01:04:52,351 --> 01:04:54,770
to send out 20 agents
Christmas Eve

1203
01:04:54,770 --> 01:04:57,564
we barge into your hotel,
knock down the door

1204
01:04:57,564 --> 01:04:59,816
so you can make fools
out of us all.

1205
01:04:59,816 --> 01:05:02,236
I'm really sorry
if I made a fool out of you.

1206
01:05:02,236 --> 01:05:03,403
I really am.

1207
01:05:03,403 --> 01:05:04,446
Uh-uh, no.

1208
01:05:04,446 --> 01:05:05,822
No, listen, I really am.

1209
01:05:05,822 --> 01:05:08,200
No, no, you-you do not
feel sorry for me.

1210
01:05:08,200 --> 01:05:10,536
The truth is,
I knew it was you.

1211
01:05:10,536 --> 01:05:13,080
Now maybe I didn't get the cuffs
on you, but I knew.

1212
01:05:13,080 --> 01:05:17,251
Ah, people only know
what you tell them, Carl.

1213
01:05:17,251 --> 01:05:20,879
Well, then tell me this,
Barry Allen, secret service.

1214
01:05:20,879 --> 01:05:24,174
How did you know
I wouldn't look in your wallet?

1215
01:05:24,174 --> 01:05:26,844
The same reason
the Yankees always win.

1216
01:05:26,844 --> 01:05:30,013
Nobody can keep their eyes
off the pinstripes.

1217
01:05:30,013 --> 01:05:33,267
The Yankees win
because they have Mickey Mantle.

1218
01:05:33,267 --> 01:05:35,519
No one ever bets on the uniform.

1219
01:05:36,812 --> 01:05:38,647
You sure about that, Carl?

1220
01:05:38,647 --> 01:05:40,899
I'll tell you what I am sure of.

1221
01:05:40,899 --> 01:05:42,860
You're going to get caught.

1222
01:05:42,860 --> 01:05:45,988
One way or another,
it's a mathematical fact.

1223
01:05:45,988 --> 01:05:47,489
It's-It's like Vegas.

1224
01:05:47,489 --> 01:05:48,866
The House always wins.

1225
01:05:54,454 --> 01:05:58,333
Well, Carl, I'm sorry,
but I have to go.

1226
01:05:58,333 --> 01:06:01,253
Ah. You didn't call
just to apologize, did you?

1227
01:06:02,462 --> 01:06:04,840
What do you mean?

1228
01:06:04,840 --> 01:06:07,885
You... you...
you have no one else to call.

1229
01:06:11,013 --> 01:06:12,598
Oh, ho, ho.

1230
01:06:19,104 --> 01:06:21,315
...Morn and night...

1231
01:06:33,410 --> 01:06:35,037
You got that burger up?

1232
01:06:35,037 --> 01:06:36,079
Yep.

1233
01:06:39,041 --> 01:06:41,043
- Hi.
- Hi!

1234
01:06:41,043 --> 01:06:42,377
How are you?

1235
01:06:42,377 --> 01:06:44,129
...Doo-lang, doo-lang,
doo-lang...

1236
01:06:44,129 --> 01:06:45,964
The one
with the wavy hair...

1237
01:06:45,964 --> 01:06:47,382
More coffee, sir?

1238
01:06:53,972 --> 01:06:55,140
Are you a collector?

1239
01:06:55,140 --> 01:06:56,642
Of what?

1240
01:06:56,642 --> 01:06:58,727
"Captives of the Cosmic Ray,"
"The Big Freeze"

1241
01:06:58,727 --> 01:07:00,395
"Land of the Golden Giants."

1242
01:07:00,395 --> 01:07:01,438
I've got them all.

1243
01:07:01,438 --> 01:07:03,899
What are you talking about?

1244
01:07:03,899 --> 01:07:05,943
Barry Allen.

1245
01:07:07,861 --> 01:07:09,446
The Flash.

1246
01:07:11,031 --> 01:07:13,033
Wait, kid, kid, kid.

1247
01:07:15,410 --> 01:07:16,787
You mean like the comic book?

1248
01:07:16,787 --> 01:07:17,829
Yeah, the comic book.

1249
01:07:17,829 --> 01:07:19,039
When he's not The Flash.

1250
01:07:19,039 --> 01:07:20,541
That's his name, Barry Allen.

1251
01:07:20,541 --> 01:07:23,085
Thank you.

1252
01:07:27,256 --> 01:07:29,925
Now get this:
He reads comic books.

1253
01:07:29,925 --> 01:07:32,719
Comic books!
Barry Allen is The Flash!

1254
01:07:32,719 --> 01:07:34,304
Carl, slow down. Slow down.

1255
01:07:34,304 --> 01:07:35,556
I don't know what the hell
you're talking about.

1256
01:07:35,556 --> 01:07:37,224
He's a kid.
Our unsub is a kid.

1257
01:07:37,224 --> 01:07:39,142
That's why we couldn't match
his prints.

1258
01:07:39,142 --> 01:07:40,853
That's why he doesn't have
a record.

1259
01:07:40,853 --> 01:07:42,355
Now, I want you to contact NYPD

1260
01:07:42,355 --> 01:07:45,399
for every all-points juvenile
runaways in New York City.

1261
01:07:45,399 --> 01:07:46,567
And don't forget the airports.

1262
01:07:46,567 --> 01:07:48,610
He's been kiting checks
all over the country.

1263
01:07:48,610 --> 01:07:49,987
But why New York?

1264
01:07:49,987 --> 01:07:50,988
The Yankees!

1265
01:07:50,988 --> 01:07:53,615
He said something
about the Yankees!

1266
01:07:54,992 --> 01:07:57,661
so where are we on the list?

1267
01:07:58,662 --> 01:08:00,831
Number 53, "Abagnahlee."

1268
01:08:03,208 --> 01:08:04,418
Good morning, ma'am.

1269
01:08:04,418 --> 01:08:05,711
We're the FBI agents
who called.

1270
01:08:05,711 --> 01:08:07,254
Yes, I've been waiting.

1271
01:08:07,254 --> 01:08:09,173
I hope you're all hungry.

1272
01:08:09,173 --> 01:08:10,757
I put out the sara Lee.

1273
01:08:13,760 --> 01:08:16,096
My husband Jack is a lawyer.

1274
01:08:16,096 --> 01:08:19,141
What about your first husband,
Mrs. "Abagnahlee"?

1275
01:08:19,141 --> 01:08:22,853
Abagnale, but I prefer
to be called Barnes.

1276
01:08:24,396 --> 01:08:26,273
"Frank William Abagnale."

1277
01:08:26,273 --> 01:08:28,025
It says here
he was in the service.

1278
01:08:28,025 --> 01:08:29,985
Did... Did you two meet
during the war?

1279
01:08:29,985 --> 01:08:32,779
Yeah, I lived
in a very small village

1280
01:08:32,779 --> 01:08:36,074
in France... Montrichard...
the kind of place

1281
01:08:36,074 --> 01:08:38,785
where they never heard
of sara Lee.

1282
01:08:38,785 --> 01:08:40,454
Help yourselves.

1283
01:08:40,454 --> 01:08:42,539
"Nobody doesn't like sara Lee."

1284
01:08:42,539 --> 01:08:44,750
You filled out
a missing person's report

1285
01:08:44,750 --> 01:08:48,045
for a runaway juvenile by
the name of Frank Abagnale Jr.

1286
01:08:48,045 --> 01:08:49,630
Is Frankie okay?

1287
01:08:49,630 --> 01:08:51,840
You're aware of the fact
that he wrote some checks

1288
01:08:51,840 --> 01:08:53,800
on a closed account
at Chase Manhattan Bank?

1289
01:08:53,800 --> 01:08:55,302
Oh, yes.

1290
01:08:55,302 --> 01:08:57,930
The police think
he's some type of criminal.

1291
01:08:57,930 --> 01:09:00,599
What he did was a felony,
Mrs. Barnes.

1292
01:09:00,599 --> 01:09:02,434
It was $1,000.

1293
01:09:02,434 --> 01:09:05,646
Half the kids his age are
on dope

1294
01:09:05,646 --> 01:09:08,232
throwing rocks at police

1295
01:09:08,232 --> 01:09:09,858
and they scared me to death

1296
01:09:09,858 --> 01:09:12,110
because my son made
a little mistake.

1297
01:09:12,110 --> 01:09:16,114
Huh. A 17-year-old...
boy has to eat

1298
01:09:16,114 --> 01:09:18,283
has to have a place to sleep.

1299
01:09:18,283 --> 01:09:20,994
We understand, ma'am.

1300
01:09:20,994 --> 01:09:22,663
Would you happen to have
a picture of your son?

1301
01:09:22,663 --> 01:09:24,623
Oh, yes.
I have his old yearbook.

1302
01:09:33,632 --> 01:09:35,634
Okay.

1303
01:09:35,634 --> 01:09:37,553
Okay, okay, we, uh...

1304
01:09:37,553 --> 01:09:40,597
we need to send out
an all-office teletype.

1305
01:09:40,597 --> 01:09:44,017
Our unsub's name is
Frank Abagnale Jr., age 17.

1306
01:09:44,017 --> 01:09:46,270
Is Frankie okay?
Is he in trouble?

1307
01:09:46,270 --> 01:09:47,896
Ma'am, I'm sorry
to have to tell you:

1308
01:09:47,896 --> 01:09:49,064
Your son is forging checks.

1309
01:09:49,064 --> 01:09:50,816
Forging checks? Wait!

1310
01:09:50,816 --> 01:09:52,317
I'm sure we can take care
of that.

1311
01:09:52,317 --> 01:09:54,236
I am working part-time
at the church now.

1312
01:09:54,236 --> 01:09:56,738
Just tell me how much he owes
and I'll pay you back.

1313
01:09:56,738 --> 01:09:59,616
so far, it's about $1.3 million.

1314
01:10:06,498 --> 01:10:08,417
Girl, you really
got me goin'

1315
01:10:08,417 --> 01:10:11,545
You got me so
I don't know what I'm doin'

1316
01:10:12,838 --> 01:10:14,339
Yeah, you really
got me goin'

1317
01:10:14,339 --> 01:10:16,342
You got me
so I can't sleep at night...

1318
01:10:16,342 --> 01:10:18,343
Hi, Melanie, how are you?

1319
01:10:18,343 --> 01:10:20,679
When you're in the house,
please, just use an ashtray.

1320
01:10:20,679 --> 01:10:22,723
Frank, this fondue is so good!

1321
01:10:22,723 --> 01:10:24,474
Great. Here, take this for me.

1322
01:10:24,474 --> 01:10:26,018
Ooh, good! I love Moet!

1323
01:10:26,018 --> 01:10:27,019
Oh, yeah...

1324
01:10:27,019 --> 01:10:29,021
Hey. How are you?

1325
01:10:29,021 --> 01:10:30,564
You really got me goin'

1326
01:10:30,564 --> 01:10:32,649
You got me goin',
got me goin' and goin'...

1327
01:10:34,693 --> 01:10:36,320
James, James, please!

1328
01:10:36,320 --> 01:10:38,322
Just stay away from the
hi-fi system, all right?

1329
01:10:38,322 --> 01:10:39,323
It's reel-to-reel.

1330
01:10:39,323 --> 01:10:40,866
You can't wind it like that.

1331
01:10:40,866 --> 01:10:42,826
Don't ever set me free...

1332
01:10:44,203 --> 01:10:46,371
Christ! Terry!

1333
01:10:46,371 --> 01:10:47,706
This is Italian knit!

1334
01:10:47,706 --> 01:10:48,708
Watch where you're going!

1335
01:10:48,708 --> 01:10:50,209
It's just a shirt, man!

1336
01:10:50,209 --> 01:10:52,794
Frank! Come quick!

1337
01:10:52,794 --> 01:10:56,256
Lance just fell
into the conversation pit!

1338
01:11:01,178 --> 01:11:04,097
Excuse me, you know
where Lance Applebaum is?

1339
01:11:04,097 --> 01:11:05,891
Thank you.

1340
01:11:05,891 --> 01:11:08,644
These bottles need to be labeled
when you pick them up.

1341
01:11:08,644 --> 01:11:10,229
Do you understand
how dangerous this is?

1342
01:11:10,229 --> 01:11:12,064
Do you?

1343
01:11:12,064 --> 01:11:13,899
Don't stand there crying,
just nod your head

1344
01:11:13,899 --> 01:11:15,317
and tell me
you won't do it again.

1345
01:11:15,317 --> 01:11:17,236
Now dry up and get back to work.

1346
01:11:17,236 --> 01:11:19,780
Dr. Blair, Dr. Blair

1347
01:11:19,780 --> 01:11:21,031
Dr. Sherwood Blair.

1348
01:11:21,031 --> 01:11:24,826
Hey, hey... you okay?

1349
01:11:24,826 --> 01:11:27,412
He told me to pick up the blood,

1350
01:11:27,412 --> 01:11:29,873
so I did, but he never told me
to label it.

1351
01:11:29,873 --> 01:11:31,875
Hey, it's okay.

1352
01:11:31,875 --> 01:11:34,127
stop crying.

1353
01:11:34,127 --> 01:11:36,213
What's your name?

1354
01:11:36,213 --> 01:11:38,924
- Brenda.
- Brenda.

1355
01:11:38,924 --> 01:11:41,093
Brenda, I wouldn't worry
about it.

1356
01:11:41,093 --> 01:11:42,595
You know, these doctors

1357
01:11:42,595 --> 01:11:45,013
you know,
they don't know everything.

1358
01:11:45,013 --> 01:11:46,557
It's my first week

1359
01:11:46,557 --> 01:11:49,434
and I think they're
going to fire me.

1360
01:11:49,434 --> 01:11:52,896
No, no, nobody's
going to fire you, Brenda.

1361
01:11:52,896 --> 01:11:55,275
I bet you're good at your job.

1362
01:11:55,275 --> 01:11:57,359
No, I'm not.

1363
01:11:57,359 --> 01:12:00,821
Yeah, I bet if I asked you
to check on the status

1364
01:12:00,821 --> 01:12:02,906
of my friend Lance Applebaum

1365
01:12:02,906 --> 01:12:05,450
that you could do that for me
in a second.

1366
01:12:05,450 --> 01:12:08,453
Nurse Fitzsimmons to Recovery.

1367
01:12:08,453 --> 01:12:10,080
Nurse Fitzsimmons to Recovery.

1368
01:12:10,789 --> 01:12:13,542
Um...

1369
01:12:13,542 --> 01:12:16,545
Mr. Applebaum fractured
his ankle.

1370
01:12:16,545 --> 01:12:19,966
Dr. Ashland is treating him
in exam room seven.

1371
01:12:19,966 --> 01:12:23,635
You see that? No problem.

1372
01:12:25,262 --> 01:12:27,890
This is the emergency chart.

1373
01:12:27,890 --> 01:12:29,433
see that blue star there?

1374
01:12:29,433 --> 01:12:32,269
That means that the patient
has been diagnosed.

1375
01:12:32,269 --> 01:12:34,146
And then,
after he's been treated

1376
01:12:34,146 --> 01:12:37,691
we put a red circle here, see?

1377
01:12:37,691 --> 01:12:39,359
How do you like those braces?

1378
01:12:43,930 --> 01:12:45,824
I got mine off last year.

1379
01:12:47,142 --> 01:12:49,853
Boy, I hated them.
They were bottoms.

1380
01:12:49,853 --> 01:12:53,189
You know, I still got to wear
my mouth guard.

1381
01:12:53,189 --> 01:12:55,400
You have really nice teeth.

1382
01:12:56,401 --> 01:12:58,611
Well, thank you.

1383
01:12:58,611 --> 01:13:01,948
And you have a pretty smile.

1384
01:13:01,948 --> 01:13:03,825
Custodial to cafeteria.

1385
01:13:05,118 --> 01:13:06,286
No, I mean it.

1386
01:13:06,286 --> 01:13:08,371
I really think
those braces look good on you.

1387
01:13:08,371 --> 01:13:10,373
Thank you.

1388
01:13:10,373 --> 01:13:12,709
You're welcome.

1389
01:13:15,295 --> 01:13:16,754
Brenda.

1390
01:13:16,754 --> 01:13:18,047
Yeah.

1391
01:13:18,047 --> 01:13:21,050
Do you know if they're hiring
here at the hospital?

1392
01:13:22,385 --> 01:13:24,137
I'm not sure.

1393
01:13:24,137 --> 01:13:25,764
What do you want to do?

1394
01:13:25,764 --> 01:13:29,601
I'm a doctor.

1395
01:13:32,145 --> 01:13:33,855
Dear Dad:

1396
01:13:33,855 --> 01:13:36,232
I've decided to get
off the road for awhile.

1397
01:13:36,232 --> 01:13:38,610
I've taken a night job
at a hospital

1398
01:13:38,610 --> 01:13:40,361
and met
some really nice people.

1399
01:13:40,361 --> 01:13:42,572
Feels good to have my feet
on the ground

1400
01:13:42,572 --> 01:13:46,242
to wake up in the same bed
every night.

1401
01:13:46,242 --> 01:13:50,246
Who knows, maybe I'll even find
someone to settle down with.

1402
01:13:52,916 --> 01:13:54,959
Harvard Medical school...

1403
01:13:54,959 --> 01:13:57,337
top of your class.

1404
01:13:57,337 --> 01:14:00,465
southern California
Children's Hospital.

1405
01:14:00,465 --> 01:14:04,177
Well, that's a pretty impressive
resume, Dr. Conners

1406
01:14:04,177 --> 01:14:07,472
but unfortunately, uh...
the only thing I need

1407
01:14:07,472 --> 01:14:10,892
is a...
an emergency room supervisor

1408
01:14:10,892 --> 01:14:13,978
for my midnight to: :00am shift

1409
01:14:13,978 --> 01:14:18,358
someone to baby-sit
six interns and 20 nurses

1410
01:14:18,358 --> 01:14:21,236
but, uh...

1411
01:14:21,236 --> 01:14:25,281
Hell, I doubt that, uh,
you would be interested in that.

1412
01:14:25,281 --> 01:14:27,826
Well, in the past

1413
01:14:27,826 --> 01:14:31,871
they've always let me choose
my own nurses.

1414
01:14:31,871 --> 01:14:34,666
Dr. Connelly?

1415
01:14:34,666 --> 01:14:35,875
Dr. Harris?

1416
01:14:35,875 --> 01:14:37,085
Present.

1417
01:14:37,085 --> 01:14:38,837
Dr. Ashland?

1418
01:14:38,837 --> 01:14:40,505
Dr. Conners...

1419
01:14:40,505 --> 01:14:42,841
You gonna take roll every night?

1420
01:14:42,841 --> 01:14:44,717
Uh, yes, I will, Dr. Ashland

1421
01:14:44,717 --> 01:14:48,680
and if you're going to be late,
I suggest you bring a note.

1422
01:14:51,933 --> 01:14:54,144
Miss Basmann.

1423
01:14:54,144 --> 01:14:55,895
Miss Mace.

1424
01:14:55,895 --> 01:14:57,564
Miss strong.

1425
01:14:57,564 --> 01:14:59,023
Here.

1426
01:14:59,023 --> 01:15:01,192
Nurse Brown.

1427
01:15:01,192 --> 01:15:03,278
- Nurse sanford?
- Here.

1428
01:15:03,278 --> 01:15:05,321
30 milligrams of codeine

1429
01:15:05,321 --> 01:15:06,322
every four hours.

1430
01:15:06,322 --> 01:15:07,949
Run the plasma
at 60 drops a minute

1431
01:15:07,949 --> 01:15:09,951
until we calculate
the fluid requirements.

1432
01:15:09,951 --> 01:15:11,953
What do you estimate
the degree and extent

1433
01:15:11,953 --> 01:15:13,079
of the burns, Kildare?

1434
01:15:13,079 --> 01:15:14,789
second and third-degree burns

1435
01:15:14,789 --> 01:15:16,499
over about 20 percent
of the body surface.

1436
01:15:16,499 --> 01:15:17,500
Do you concur?

1437
01:15:17,500 --> 01:15:18,501
I concur.

1438
01:15:18,501 --> 01:15:20,545
Let's get him up to Pediatrics.

1439
01:15:20,545 --> 01:15:24,048
Nurse Hopp
to the Nurses' station south.

1440
01:15:24,048 --> 01:15:26,885
Nurse Hopp
to the Nurses' station south.

1441
01:15:26,885 --> 01:15:28,344
Hello, Brenda.

1442
01:15:28,344 --> 01:15:29,679
Hi, Dr. Conners.

1443
01:15:29,679 --> 01:15:31,723
You need to sign these.

1444
01:15:31,723 --> 01:15:33,683
Thank you.

1445
01:15:39,481 --> 01:15:41,816
Do you notice anything
different about me, Doctor?

1446
01:15:41,816 --> 01:15:43,693
- You got your braces off!
- Yeah!

1447
01:15:43,693 --> 01:15:44,903
Come here. Let me see.

1448
01:15:44,903 --> 01:15:46,696
I've been trying
to show you all night!

1449
01:15:47,947 --> 01:15:50,450
Wow. Good job.

1450
01:15:50,450 --> 01:15:51,534
Yeah?

1451
01:15:51,534 --> 01:15:52,619
so, did it hurt
when they took them off?

1452
01:15:52,619 --> 01:15:54,120
Mine felt so weird after.

1453
01:15:54,120 --> 01:15:55,581
Mm, I keep rubbing my tongue
over them.

1454
01:15:55,581 --> 01:15:58,458
I can't stop.
They're so slippery.

1455
01:15:58,458 --> 01:15:59,959
It feels good, though,
doesn't it?

1456
01:15:59,959 --> 01:16:01,961
Yeah, it feels incredible.

1457
01:16:11,638 --> 01:16:13,181
Oh, my.

1458
01:16:13,181 --> 01:16:15,642
I'm... I'm sorry.

1459
01:16:27,112 --> 01:16:29,364
Dr. Conners to the ER.

1460
01:16:29,364 --> 01:16:31,074
Dr. Conners to the ER.

1461
01:16:31,074 --> 01:16:32,283
shouldn't you go?

1462
01:16:32,283 --> 01:16:34,119
No. No, no.

1463
01:16:34,119 --> 01:16:36,121
They have a staff doctor
in the emergency ward.

1464
01:16:36,121 --> 01:16:38,123
We'll be fine.

1465
01:16:42,585 --> 01:16:45,839
What if he's in surgery?

1466
01:16:45,839 --> 01:16:49,008
Do you really think
I have to go?

1467
01:16:49,008 --> 01:16:51,636
Oh. In here, Dr. Conners.

1468
01:17:07,986 --> 01:17:12,031
Gentlemen, what, uh...
what seems to be the problem?

1469
01:17:12,031 --> 01:17:13,408
Bicycle accident.

1470
01:17:13,408 --> 01:17:17,537
Fractured tibia about
five inches below the patella.

1471
01:17:17,537 --> 01:17:19,497
Hmm.

1472
01:17:22,000 --> 01:17:24,169
- Dr. Harris.
- Yes?

1473
01:17:24,169 --> 01:17:25,253
Do you concur?

1474
01:17:25,253 --> 01:17:28,674
C... Concur with what, sir?

1475
01:17:28,674 --> 01:17:30,676
With what Dr. Ashland just said.

1476
01:17:30,676 --> 01:17:33,344
Do you... Do you concur?

1477
01:17:33,344 --> 01:17:35,681
Uh... well, it was
a bicycle accident.

1478
01:17:35,681 --> 01:17:37,682
Um, the boy told us.

1479
01:17:37,682 --> 01:17:39,267
so you concur?

1480
01:17:39,267 --> 01:17:41,311
Concur? Uh...

1481
01:17:41,311 --> 01:17:42,604
I think we should take an X ray

1482
01:17:42,604 --> 01:17:45,356
then stitch him up
and put him in a walking cast.

1483
01:17:48,651 --> 01:17:50,945
That's very good, Dr. Ashland.
Very good.

1484
01:17:50,945 --> 01:17:53,699
Well, you don't seem
to have much need for me.

1485
01:17:53,699 --> 01:17:55,366
Carry on.

1486
01:17:57,243 --> 01:18:00,039
I blew it, didn't I?

1487
01:18:00,039 --> 01:18:02,248
Why didn't I concur?

1488
01:18:02,248 --> 01:18:05,335
Dr. Henning, call extension 219.

1489
01:18:05,335 --> 01:18:06,878
Dr. Henning, extension 219.

1490
01:18:23,978 --> 01:18:25,313
Make yourself at home!

1491
01:18:25,313 --> 01:18:28,316
Frank Abagnale sr.

1492
01:18:28,316 --> 01:18:30,777
You're not a cop.

1493
01:18:30,777 --> 01:18:34,614
special Agent Hanratty, FBI.

1494
01:18:34,614 --> 01:18:35,657
You're not a cop.

1495
01:18:35,657 --> 01:18:38,159
My landlord said
you were not a cop.

1496
01:18:38,159 --> 01:18:39,786
Well, if you're going
to arrest me

1497
01:18:39,786 --> 01:18:41,454
I'd like
to put on a different suit

1498
01:18:41,454 --> 01:18:42,664
if that's okay with you.

1499
01:18:42,664 --> 01:18:44,332
No, no, I'm not here
to arrest you.

1500
01:18:44,332 --> 01:18:46,417
I'm looking for your son.
He's in trouble.

1501
01:18:46,417 --> 01:18:47,836
Do you know where he is?

1502
01:18:50,630 --> 01:18:51,881
If I tell you where he is

1503
01:18:51,881 --> 01:18:53,883
will you promise
not to tell his mother?

1504
01:18:53,883 --> 01:18:55,635
sure.

1505
01:18:55,635 --> 01:18:59,139
Frank made up a fake I.D.

1506
01:18:59,139 --> 01:19:00,599
and enlisted
in the Marine Corps.

1507
01:19:00,599 --> 01:19:02,100
He's over in Vietnam right now.

1508
01:19:02,100 --> 01:19:04,394
That kid is halfway
around the world

1509
01:19:04,394 --> 01:19:06,479
crawling through the damn jungle

1510
01:19:06,479 --> 01:19:08,940
fighting the Communists, so...

1511
01:19:11,151 --> 01:19:14,779
please, don't come to my home
and call my boy a criminal

1512
01:19:14,779 --> 01:19:16,156
because that kid has
more guts...

1513
01:19:16,156 --> 01:19:18,116
I never said he was a criminal,
Mr. Abagnale.

1514
01:19:18,116 --> 01:19:19,868
I said he was in trouble.

1515
01:19:19,868 --> 01:19:23,246
If you'd like to give me a call
and talk, here's my number.

1516
01:19:35,633 --> 01:19:37,469
You're not a father, are you?

1517
01:19:39,637 --> 01:19:42,015
Pardon me?

1518
01:19:42,015 --> 01:19:43,476
If you were a father,
you'd know.

1519
01:19:43,476 --> 01:19:46,978
I would never give up my son.

1520
01:19:46,978 --> 01:19:50,649
I would never give up my son.

1521
01:19:50,649 --> 01:19:54,110
Yes, sir. I understand.

1522
01:19:54,110 --> 01:19:56,322
sean, sean, now get this:

1523
01:19:56,322 --> 01:19:57,781
"Riverbend Apartments

1524
01:19:57,781 --> 01:20:01,326
415 Landover, Atlanta, Georgia."

1525
01:20:01,326 --> 01:20:02,744
Atlanta, Georgia.

1526
01:20:02,744 --> 01:20:04,454
Yeah, I'm on my way
to the airport.

1527
01:20:04,454 --> 01:20:06,998
I'll meet the team in, uh,
in four hours.

1528
01:20:06,998 --> 01:20:08,041
Bye-bye.

1529
01:20:10,293 --> 01:20:11,795
Come on, it's okay.

1530
01:20:13,379 --> 01:20:15,340
You don't have to cry.

1531
01:20:15,340 --> 01:20:16,591
I'm sorry.

1532
01:20:16,591 --> 01:20:18,468
I'm so sorry, Frank.

1533
01:20:18,468 --> 01:20:19,969
I can't do this.

1534
01:20:19,969 --> 01:20:22,514
Brenda, listen to me.

1535
01:20:22,514 --> 01:20:24,850
I don't care if you're
a virgin, all right?

1536
01:20:24,850 --> 01:20:26,059
Really, I can wait.

1537
01:20:26,059 --> 01:20:29,187
I'm not a virgin.

1538
01:20:33,149 --> 01:20:35,777
I had an abortion two years ago.

1539
01:20:38,196 --> 01:20:42,575
My parents had a friend do it

1540
01:20:42,575 --> 01:20:46,872
a man that my father
plays golf with.

1541
01:20:46,872 --> 01:20:51,209
And then, when I got better,
they kicked me out of the house.

1542
01:20:51,209 --> 01:20:54,087
I had an abortion and I wasn't
their daughter anymore.

1543
01:20:54,087 --> 01:20:55,588
Hey...

1544
01:20:55,588 --> 01:20:56,589
I'm so sorry.

1545
01:20:56,589 --> 01:20:58,216
Please don't be mad at me.

1546
01:20:58,216 --> 01:21:00,385
Please, please,
don't be mad at me.

1547
01:21:00,385 --> 01:21:01,511
No, no.

1548
01:21:01,511 --> 01:21:03,346
Please don't be mad at me.

1549
01:21:03,346 --> 01:21:05,223
shh. Now... what if...

1550
01:21:05,223 --> 01:21:08,518
what if I spoke
to your parents, right?

1551
01:21:08,518 --> 01:21:10,478
May-Maybe I can
straighten things out, huh?

1552
01:21:10,478 --> 01:21:12,522
Well, I ask them all the time

1553
01:21:12,522 --> 01:21:15,191
but they said I still
can't come home.

1554
01:21:15,191 --> 01:21:19,405
And my daddy's... a lawyer.

1555
01:21:19,405 --> 01:21:21,406
Aw...

1556
01:21:26,661 --> 01:21:30,165
Brenda...

1557
01:21:30,165 --> 01:21:33,626
what if you were engaged
to a doctor?

1558
01:21:33,626 --> 01:21:35,628
Will that change anything?

1559
01:21:35,628 --> 01:21:37,255
What?

1560
01:21:40,592 --> 01:21:44,596
What if I went
to your parents...

1561
01:21:44,596 --> 01:21:46,723
and I spoke to your father...

1562
01:21:50,185 --> 01:21:53,438
and I asked permission
to marry you?

1563
01:22:06,785 --> 01:22:07,787
It's empty.

1564
01:22:07,787 --> 01:22:09,287
Nobody here.

1565
01:22:33,645 --> 01:22:36,731
Dr. Conners, are you Lutheran?

1566
01:22:36,731 --> 01:22:42,112
Yes, I-I am a Lutheran,
but, please, call me Frank.

1567
01:22:42,112 --> 01:22:44,739
Frank, would you like
to say grace?

1568
01:22:49,536 --> 01:22:53,332
Unless you're not comfortable.

1569
01:22:53,332 --> 01:22:55,333
Absolutely.

1570
01:23:04,968 --> 01:23:08,471
Two little mice fell
into a bucket of cream.

1571
01:23:10,181 --> 01:23:12,434
The first mouse quickly
gave up and drowned

1572
01:23:12,434 --> 01:23:14,687
but the second mouse,
he struggled so hard

1573
01:23:14,687 --> 01:23:17,355
that he eventually churned
that cream into butter

1574
01:23:17,355 --> 01:23:19,357
and he walked out.

1575
01:23:19,357 --> 01:23:23,529
- Amen.
- Amen.

1576
01:23:23,529 --> 01:23:26,532
Amen. Oh, that was beautiful.

1577
01:23:26,532 --> 01:23:29,159
The mouse, he churned
that cream into butter.

1578
01:23:31,870 --> 01:23:32,871
That's right.

1579
01:23:32,871 --> 01:23:34,206
That's pretty good.

1580
01:23:34,206 --> 01:23:35,957
Thank you.

1581
01:23:35,957 --> 01:23:37,710
Frank, have you decided
which hospital

1582
01:23:37,710 --> 01:23:39,586
you want to work at
here in New Orleans?

1583
01:23:39,586 --> 01:23:41,838
Well, um, to be quite honest

1584
01:23:41,838 --> 01:23:45,050
I'm thinking
about getting back into law.

1585
01:23:45,050 --> 01:23:46,885
Oh, my!

1586
01:23:46,885 --> 01:23:49,095
Are you a doctor or a lawyer?

1587
01:23:49,095 --> 01:23:52,974
Before I went to medical school,
I passed the bar in California.

1588
01:23:52,974 --> 01:23:54,559
I practiced law for one year

1589
01:23:54,559 --> 01:23:58,772
then I decided why not
try my hand at pediatrics?

1590
01:23:58,772 --> 01:24:01,608
You're just full of surprises.

1591
01:24:01,608 --> 01:24:03,443
Yeah.

1592
01:24:03,443 --> 01:24:05,069
Oh, my.

1593
01:24:05,069 --> 01:24:06,571
A doctor and a lawyer.

1594
01:24:06,571 --> 01:24:08,073
Well, I'd say that Brenda
hit the jackpot.

1595
01:24:08,073 --> 01:24:11,076
Where did you go to law school?

1596
01:24:11,076 --> 01:24:12,786
Uh, Berkeley.

1597
01:24:13,787 --> 01:24:15,246
Berkley, Berkley. Oh, my gosh.

1598
01:24:15,246 --> 01:24:16,790
Isn't that where you went,
Daddy?

1599
01:24:16,790 --> 01:24:18,751
Maybe Frank could come work
for you, Roger.

1600
01:24:18,751 --> 01:24:20,543
You're always saying
how hard it is

1601
01:24:20,543 --> 01:24:22,086
to find
Assistant Prosecutors.

1602
01:24:22,086 --> 01:24:24,339
Could he, Daddy?
Could he, please?

1603
01:24:24,339 --> 01:24:25,840
Could he come work with you,
please?

1604
01:24:25,840 --> 01:24:27,926
Was that snake Hollingsworth
still teaching there

1605
01:24:27,926 --> 01:24:29,177
when you went through Berkley?

1606
01:24:30,929 --> 01:24:32,430
Hollingsworth.

1607
01:24:32,430 --> 01:24:35,600
Yes. Grumpy old Hollingsworth,
right?

1608
01:24:35,600 --> 01:24:37,185
I tell you. Meaner than ever.

1609
01:24:37,185 --> 01:24:39,187
And that dog of his?

1610
01:24:41,773 --> 01:24:45,985
Tell me, Frank, what was
the name of his little dog?

1611
01:24:54,494 --> 01:24:57,997
I'm sorry. Uh...

1612
01:24:57,997 --> 01:24:59,958
The dog was dead.

1613
01:25:01,543 --> 01:25:05,130
How unfortunate.

1614
01:25:05,130 --> 01:25:07,090
Yeah.

1615
01:25:37,412 --> 01:25:40,206
A doctor, a lawyer,
a Lutheran...

1616
01:25:42,917 --> 01:25:45,962
so what are you, Frank?

1617
01:25:45,962 --> 01:25:47,755
'Cause I think you're
about to ask

1618
01:25:47,755 --> 01:25:49,591
for my daughter's hand
in marriage

1619
01:25:49,591 --> 01:25:51,134
and I have a right to know.

1620
01:25:51,134 --> 01:25:53,470
Know what, sir?

1621
01:25:53,470 --> 01:25:56,222
The truth.

1622
01:25:56,222 --> 01:26:00,685
Tell me the truth, Frank.

1623
01:26:00,685 --> 01:26:04,481
What are you doing here?

1624
01:26:04,481 --> 01:26:07,692
What is a man like you doing
with Brenda?

1625
01:26:07,692 --> 01:26:09,819
If you want my blessing

1626
01:26:09,819 --> 01:26:11,988
if you want my daughter

1627
01:26:11,988 --> 01:26:14,949
I'd like to hear it
from you now.

1628
01:26:17,827 --> 01:26:19,829
The truth is, sir, that...

1629
01:26:23,458 --> 01:26:25,001
The truth is that...

1630
01:26:27,253 --> 01:26:30,715
I'm not a doctor,
I'm not a lawyer...

1631
01:26:33,051 --> 01:26:35,804
I'm not an airline pilot.

1632
01:26:35,804 --> 01:26:38,807
I'm... I'm nothing, really.

1633
01:26:44,729 --> 01:26:48,525
I'm-I'm-I'm just a kid who's
in love with your daughter.

1634
01:26:51,736 --> 01:26:54,072
No.

1635
01:27:01,955 --> 01:27:04,374
You know what you are?

1636
01:27:04,374 --> 01:27:06,376
You're a romantic.

1637
01:27:06,376 --> 01:27:09,420
Men like us are nothing
without the women we love.

1638
01:27:09,420 --> 01:27:13,091
I must confess, I'm guilty
of the same foolish whimsy.

1639
01:27:13,091 --> 01:27:15,260
I proposed to Carol
after five dates

1640
01:27:15,260 --> 01:27:18,304
with two nickels in my pockets
and holes in my shoes

1641
01:27:18,304 --> 01:27:20,432
because I knew she was the one.

1642
01:27:20,432 --> 01:27:23,268
so go ahead, Frank.

1643
01:27:26,312 --> 01:27:28,398
Don't be afraid.

1644
01:27:28,398 --> 01:27:32,110
Ask the question you came here
to ask me.

1645
01:27:34,070 --> 01:27:36,614
sir, uh, uh...

1646
01:27:36,614 --> 01:27:38,158
w-what would I have to do

1647
01:27:38,158 --> 01:27:40,743
to take the bar
here in New Orleans?

1648
01:27:45,457 --> 01:27:48,918
No, the... the other question.

1649
01:27:52,464 --> 01:27:56,426
Right through that door.

1650
01:27:56,426 --> 01:27:59,304
Good luck, Mr. Conners.

1651
01:27:59,304 --> 01:28:01,097
Thank you.

1652
01:28:08,396 --> 01:28:10,106
Hey, Frank...

1653
01:28:10,106 --> 01:28:12,318
you know what I could
never figure out?

1654
01:28:12,318 --> 01:28:15,111
How did you cheat on the
bar exam in Louisiana?

1655
01:28:15,111 --> 01:28:16,946
Why? What's the difference?

1656
01:28:16,946 --> 01:28:19,324
someone else took the test
for you, didn't they?

1657
01:28:19,324 --> 01:28:22,076
Carl, I'm going to prison
for a long time.

1658
01:28:22,076 --> 01:28:24,871
seriously,
what's the difference?

1659
01:28:24,871 --> 01:28:27,166
It's a simple question.

1660
01:28:27,166 --> 01:28:29,626
Are you going to eat
that eclair?

1661
01:28:32,170 --> 01:28:35,840
Yeah. I'm saving it for later.

1662
01:28:35,840 --> 01:28:37,676
Well, you want
to split it with me?

1663
01:28:37,676 --> 01:28:41,262
No.

1664
01:28:41,262 --> 01:28:44,724
Give me half that eclair
and I'll tell you.

1665
01:28:54,275 --> 01:28:58,655
I'm going to figure it out
sooner or later.

1666
01:29:05,203 --> 01:29:08,748
You'll be working under
Phillip Rigby in corporate law.

1667
01:29:08,748 --> 01:29:11,793
Why don't you settle in,
organize your desk?

1668
01:29:14,045 --> 01:29:15,547
Thank you.

1669
01:29:15,547 --> 01:29:18,384
We're having lunch at 12:30
with the Attorney General

1670
01:29:18,384 --> 01:29:20,386
and Governor McKeithen.

1671
01:29:20,386 --> 01:29:21,720
Himself.

1672
01:29:21,720 --> 01:29:23,055
The Governor.

1673
01:29:23,055 --> 01:29:24,305
Did we spell it right?

1674
01:29:24,305 --> 01:29:25,932
You sure did.

1675
01:29:25,932 --> 01:29:27,767
Congratulations.

1676
01:29:27,767 --> 01:29:29,018
Thank you, sir.

1677
01:29:29,018 --> 01:29:30,311
Welcome aboard.

1678
01:29:30,311 --> 01:29:32,313
Now...

1679
01:29:36,734 --> 01:29:39,404
Look at this photograph,
Mr. Stewart.

1680
01:29:39,404 --> 01:29:42,575
It's a photograph
of Prentice York

1681
01:29:42,575 --> 01:29:44,701
where they found him, dead.

1682
01:29:44,701 --> 01:29:47,996
Now, here is an enlargement
of part of that photograph.

1683
01:29:47,996 --> 01:29:50,582
This is a photograph
of the defendant's signature

1684
01:29:50,582 --> 01:29:52,083
on a canceled check.

1685
01:29:52,083 --> 01:29:54,627
Now, here is an enlargement
of that same signature

1686
01:29:54,627 --> 01:29:55,837
which matches

1687
01:29:55,837 --> 01:29:58,882
the signature on the letters
that he wrote to Mrs. Simon

1688
01:29:58,882 --> 01:30:00,675
which discuss the possibility

1689
01:30:00,675 --> 01:30:03,011
of defrauding
the great state of Louisiana.

1690
01:30:03,011 --> 01:30:06,306
Your Honor,
ladies and gentlemen of the jury

1691
01:30:06,306 --> 01:30:08,016
this is irrefutable evidence

1692
01:30:08,016 --> 01:30:11,311
that the defendant is,
in fact, lying.

1693
01:30:16,024 --> 01:30:21,821
Mr. Conners, this is
a preliminary hearing.

1694
01:30:21,821 --> 01:30:25,450
There is no... defendant.

1695
01:30:25,450 --> 01:30:30,079
There is no... jury.

1696
01:30:30,079 --> 01:30:33,082
It's just me.

1697
01:30:33,082 --> 01:30:34,709
son...

1698
01:30:34,709 --> 01:30:39,130
what in the hell is wrong
with you?!

1699
01:30:39,130 --> 01:30:41,049
- Is that Mitch?

1700
01:30:41,049 --> 01:30:42,842
Roger! It's Mitch!

1701
01:30:42,842 --> 01:30:44,969
Oh, my,
I lost all track of time.

1702
01:30:44,969 --> 01:30:47,430
As studio guests
for the sing-along tonight

1703
01:30:47,430 --> 01:30:49,724
we have the children's choir
of st. Monica's Church

1704
01:30:49,724 --> 01:30:51,559
in New York City.

1705
01:30:51,559 --> 01:30:53,353
Won't you join them and the gang

1706
01:30:53,353 --> 01:30:55,647
in a few songs for the Irish?
Everybody!

1707
01:30:55,647 --> 01:30:58,316
Has anybody here seen Kelly?

1708
01:30:58,316 --> 01:31:01,236
K, E, double L, Y

1709
01:31:01,236 --> 01:31:03,780
Has anybody here seen Kelly?

1710
01:31:03,780 --> 01:31:05,865
Have you seen him smile?

1711
01:31:05,865 --> 01:31:08,493
sure his hair is red,
and his eyes are blue

1712
01:31:08,493 --> 01:31:11,162
And he's Irish
through and through

1713
01:31:11,162 --> 01:31:13,665
Has anybody here seen Kelly

1714
01:31:13,665 --> 01:31:16,167
Kelly from the Emerald Isle?

1715
01:31:16,167 --> 01:31:18,837
Has anybody here seen Kelly?

1716
01:31:18,837 --> 01:31:21,089
K, E, double L, Y

1717
01:31:21,089 --> 01:31:23,843
Has anybody here seen Kelly?

1718
01:31:23,843 --> 01:31:26,052
Have you seen him smile?

1719
01:31:26,052 --> 01:31:28,847
sure his hair is red,
and his eyes are blue

1720
01:31:28,847 --> 01:31:31,307
And he's Irish
through and through

1721
01:31:31,307 --> 01:31:33,686
Has anybody here
seen Kelly...

1722
01:31:33,686 --> 01:31:36,021
Embrace me

1723
01:31:36,021 --> 01:31:41,526
My sweet embraceable you

1724
01:31:41,526 --> 01:31:44,779
Embrace me

1725
01:31:44,779 --> 01:31:51,202
You irreplaceable you

1726
01:31:51,202 --> 01:31:54,247
Just one look at you

1727
01:31:54,247 --> 01:32:00,336
My heart grew tipsy in me

1728
01:32:00,336 --> 01:32:03,214
You and you alone

1729
01:32:03,214 --> 01:32:09,929
Bring out the gypsy in me

1730
01:32:09,929 --> 01:32:12,807
I love all

1731
01:32:12,807 --> 01:32:19,397
The many charms about you

1732
01:32:19,397 --> 01:32:22,275
Above all

1733
01:32:22,275 --> 01:32:25,820
I want my arms about you...

1734
01:32:25,820 --> 01:32:27,071
ad.

1735
01:32:28,531 --> 01:32:31,868
...Don't be
a naughty baby...

1736
01:32:31,868 --> 01:32:33,912
What are you doing here?

1737
01:32:33,912 --> 01:32:38,291
I... I-I came to see you.

1738
01:32:38,291 --> 01:32:41,419
...My sweet embraceable...

1739
01:32:41,419 --> 01:32:43,588
What are you doing
dressed like this?

1740
01:32:43,588 --> 01:32:45,548
I took a job. A government job.

1741
01:32:45,548 --> 01:32:47,008
You see what I'm doing?

1742
01:32:47,008 --> 01:32:48,761
Do you have a good lawyer?

1743
01:32:48,761 --> 01:32:51,263
Well... I sort of
am a lawyer now.

1744
01:32:51,263 --> 01:32:55,101
Look at this letter.
The IRs wants more.

1745
01:32:55,101 --> 01:32:57,603
I had a deal with them:
two penalties.

1746
01:32:57,603 --> 01:33:01,064
They ate the cake,
now they want the crumbs.

1747
01:33:01,064 --> 01:33:03,942
I want to sue them.

1748
01:33:03,942 --> 01:33:06,903
Now they want the crumbs.

1749
01:33:06,903 --> 01:33:09,030
They... Here, sit down.

1750
01:33:09,030 --> 01:33:11,658
They're trying to scare me,
intimidate me.

1751
01:33:11,658 --> 01:33:14,285
You know what?

1752
01:33:14,285 --> 01:33:17,705
You know what?
I'll make them chase me...

1753
01:33:17,705 --> 01:33:20,125
for the rest of their lives.

1754
01:33:26,172 --> 01:33:29,926
Hey, it's great
to see you, Daddy.

1755
01:33:29,926 --> 01:33:34,305
Listen, sit down, I...
I want to show you something.

1756
01:33:36,099 --> 01:33:38,476
I came here to give you this.

1757
01:33:38,476 --> 01:33:42,689
It's an invitation
to an engagement party.

1758
01:33:43,773 --> 01:33:46,652
Daddy, I'm getting married.

1759
01:33:46,652 --> 01:33:49,654
Can you believe that?
I'm getting married.

1760
01:33:49,654 --> 01:33:52,240
You don't need to worry
about anything now, Dad.

1761
01:33:52,240 --> 01:33:54,492
Listen, I'm getting
a brand-new Cadillac.

1762
01:33:54,492 --> 01:33:56,327
I'm getting a $60,000 house.

1763
01:33:56,327 --> 01:33:58,329
I'm-I'm getting it all back.

1764
01:33:58,329 --> 01:34:00,832
All-All the jewelry,
all the furs, everything, Dad.

1765
01:34:00,832 --> 01:34:03,585
Everything they took from us,
I'm going to get it back.

1766
01:34:03,585 --> 01:34:05,503
Now...

1767
01:34:05,503 --> 01:34:09,257
has Ma seen you
dressed like this?

1768
01:34:09,257 --> 01:34:12,760
Yeah, she came
to pick up some boxes.

1769
01:34:12,760 --> 01:34:14,429
That's okay, that's okay,
you know why?

1770
01:34:14,429 --> 01:34:16,514
'Cause she... she's going
to the wedding with us.

1771
01:34:16,514 --> 01:34:18,391
I'm going to get you
a brand-new suit, Dad.

1772
01:34:18,391 --> 01:34:20,310
I'm getting you
a brand-new suit.

1773
01:34:20,310 --> 01:34:22,520
One of those Manhattan Eagle,
three-button, black pearl suits.

1774
01:34:22,520 --> 01:34:23,563
You'll look great.

1775
01:34:23,563 --> 01:34:25,024
Those are nice. Yeah.

1776
01:34:25,024 --> 01:34:27,650
she won't see me.

1777
01:34:28,693 --> 01:34:30,570
Well, have you tried
to call her?

1778
01:34:30,570 --> 01:34:32,739
Uh-uh.

1779
01:34:32,739 --> 01:34:35,325
Why don't... why don't you
call her right now?

1780
01:34:35,325 --> 01:34:37,827
Dad, why don't you
call her right now? Here.

1781
01:34:37,827 --> 01:34:40,371
Dad, just call her.
Call her for me.

1782
01:34:40,371 --> 01:34:42,123
You call her, and you tell her

1783
01:34:42,123 --> 01:34:44,877
I have two first-class tickets
to go see her son's wedding...

1784
01:34:44,877 --> 01:34:47,545
Your mother's married now,
to my friend Jack Barnes.

1785
01:34:47,545 --> 01:34:50,590
They have a house
in Long Island.

1786
01:34:50,590 --> 01:34:54,385
I had an FBI agent come see me.

1787
01:34:54,385 --> 01:34:56,222
You got their number, son.

1788
01:34:56,222 --> 01:34:58,389
The guy looked scared.

1789
01:34:58,389 --> 01:35:02,894
The United states government,
champ, running for the hills.

1790
01:35:02,894 --> 01:35:05,188
Pow! To the moon!

1791
01:35:16,366 --> 01:35:19,244
Dad... it's over.

1792
01:35:20,745 --> 01:35:22,747
I'm going to stop now.

1793
01:35:22,747 --> 01:35:24,833
But y-you've...

1794
01:35:24,833 --> 01:35:27,043
They're never going
to catch you, Frank.

1795
01:35:27,043 --> 01:35:29,254
- Dad, she wouldn't do that.
- Why won't you sit down?

1796
01:35:29,254 --> 01:35:31,256
- Why would she do that to you?
- Come on, sit.

1797
01:35:31,256 --> 01:35:32,924
Come on, sit with me.
Have a drink.

1798
01:35:32,924 --> 01:35:34,260
I'm your father.

1799
01:35:34,260 --> 01:35:37,762
Then ask me to stop.

1800
01:35:37,762 --> 01:35:39,973
Then ask me to stop.

1801
01:35:42,851 --> 01:35:44,853
You can't stop.

1802
01:35:46,980 --> 01:35:48,815
Where are you going?

1803
01:35:48,815 --> 01:35:51,276
Come on, Frank,
where are you going?

1804
01:35:51,276 --> 01:35:52,694
Where are you going?

1805
01:35:52,694 --> 01:35:54,696
Where are you going tonight?

1806
01:35:54,696 --> 01:35:55,905
someplace exotic?

1807
01:35:55,905 --> 01:35:57,282
Where are you going tonight?

1808
01:35:57,282 --> 01:35:58,408
Tahiti, Hawaii?

1809
01:36:16,259 --> 01:36:19,179
This is Hanratty.

1810
01:36:19,179 --> 01:36:21,264
Hello, Carl.

1811
01:36:21,264 --> 01:36:23,266
Merry Christmas.

1812
01:36:23,266 --> 01:36:25,644
How are you, Dr. Conners?

1813
01:36:25,644 --> 01:36:30,106
Carl, I haven't been Dr. Conners
for months now.

1814
01:36:31,983 --> 01:36:36,863
Well... I'm sitting here
in my office on Christmas Eve.

1815
01:36:36,863 --> 01:36:38,448
What do you want?

1816
01:36:42,827 --> 01:36:45,622
Okay.

1817
01:36:49,918 --> 01:36:52,170
I want it to be over.

1818
01:36:55,340 --> 01:36:57,717
Uh... I want it to be over.

1819
01:36:57,717 --> 01:36:59,677
I'm getting married.

1820
01:36:59,677 --> 01:37:01,679
You know, I'm settling down.

1821
01:37:01,679 --> 01:37:03,682
You've stolen almost $4 million.

1822
01:37:03,682 --> 01:37:06,059
You think we can just
call that a wedding present?

1823
01:37:06,059 --> 01:37:09,104
Nah, this isn't something you
get to walk away from, Frank.

1824
01:37:09,104 --> 01:37:10,605
I want to call a truce.

1825
01:37:10,605 --> 01:37:11,773
No truce.

1826
01:37:11,773 --> 01:37:13,733
You will be caught,
you will go to prison.

1827
01:37:13,733 --> 01:37:15,360
Where did you think
this was going?

1828
01:37:15,360 --> 01:37:18,780
Please leave me alone, Carl.

1829
01:37:18,780 --> 01:37:20,198
Please?

1830
01:37:20,198 --> 01:37:22,034
I'm getting close, aren't I?

1831
01:37:22,034 --> 01:37:24,202
You're scared because
I'm getting close.

1832
01:37:24,202 --> 01:37:27,455
I know you... you rented
that car in shreveport

1833
01:37:27,455 --> 01:37:30,458
and you stayed in that hotel
on Lake Charles.

1834
01:37:30,458 --> 01:37:32,502
You want to run, be my guest.

1835
01:37:32,502 --> 01:37:34,879
Your checks don't lie
as well as you do.

1836
01:37:34,879 --> 01:37:37,841
stop chasing me.

1837
01:37:40,051 --> 01:37:42,762
I can't stop.

1838
01:37:42,762 --> 01:37:45,348
It's my job.

1839
01:37:45,348 --> 01:37:47,851
It's okay, Carl.

1840
01:37:47,851 --> 01:37:51,271
I just thought I'd ask,
you know?

1841
01:37:53,731 --> 01:37:57,777
Hey. Merry Christmas, huh?

1842
01:38:01,072 --> 01:38:03,575
I love my job.

1843
01:38:03,575 --> 01:38:05,243
All right...

1844
01:38:05,243 --> 01:38:06,744
let's get every newspaper
we can

1845
01:38:06,744 --> 01:38:09,289
every newspaper in Louisiana
for the last two months.

1846
01:38:09,289 --> 01:38:10,583
What are we looking for?

1847
01:38:10,583 --> 01:38:12,959
Engagement announcements,
name of Conners.

1848
01:38:12,959 --> 01:38:15,378
Conners?! Come on, Carl,
the kid would've

1849
01:38:15,378 --> 01:38:16,921
changed his name by now.

1850
01:38:16,921 --> 01:38:19,716
Mm-mm. He can't change it.

1851
01:38:19,716 --> 01:38:21,594
she thinks he's Conners.

1852
01:38:21,594 --> 01:38:23,845
If he loses the name,
he loses the girl.

1853
01:38:23,845 --> 01:38:25,638
I can't give you anything

1854
01:38:25,638 --> 01:38:29,350
But love, baby

1855
01:38:29,350 --> 01:38:33,229
That's the only thing
I have plenty of

1856
01:38:33,229 --> 01:38:34,314
Baby

1857
01:38:34,314 --> 01:38:36,024
Dreamin' a while,
schemin' a while...

1858
01:38:36,024 --> 01:38:37,692
- Congratulations.
- You having a good time?

1859
01:38:37,692 --> 01:38:41,113
...You're sure to find

1860
01:38:41,113 --> 01:38:43,698
- Happiness, and I guess
- Keep dancing, huh?

1861
01:38:43,698 --> 01:38:45,784
All those things
you've always pined for...

1862
01:38:45,784 --> 01:38:47,786
- Oh.
- Hi.

1863
01:38:47,786 --> 01:38:48,787
Oh, me too. Thank you.

1864
01:38:48,787 --> 01:38:50,663
I'm going to, uh,
the little boys' room.

1865
01:38:50,663 --> 01:38:51,873
- Okay.
- Okay.

1866
01:38:51,873 --> 01:38:53,416
Hurry back.

1867
01:39:07,972 --> 01:39:09,140
Good evening.

1868
01:39:09,140 --> 01:39:11,101
I'm Agent Hanratty
with the FBI.

1869
01:39:11,101 --> 01:39:13,144
We'd like to have
a few quiet words

1870
01:39:13,144 --> 01:39:14,480
with your host, if possible.

1871
01:39:14,480 --> 01:39:16,481
I'll get him.

1872
01:39:17,649 --> 01:39:19,109
Right over there, sir.

1873
01:39:19,109 --> 01:39:21,694
- Hi, Roger. How are you?
- Hi, Vin.

1874
01:39:21,694 --> 01:39:24,072
Good evening, gentlemen.
I'm Roger strong.

1875
01:39:24,072 --> 01:39:25,657
Carl Hanratty, FBI.

1876
01:39:25,657 --> 01:39:27,826
This is Agents Amdursky and Fox.

1877
01:39:27,826 --> 01:39:29,994
sorry to crash your party, sir.

1878
01:39:29,994 --> 01:39:31,996
Not at all.
What can I do for you?

1879
01:39:31,996 --> 01:39:35,375
If it's not too much trouble,
I'd like to meet the groom.

1880
01:39:35,375 --> 01:39:38,419
Is there a problem?

1881
01:39:38,419 --> 01:39:40,172
- Frank! Frank!

1882
01:39:40,172 --> 01:39:41,840
Can you hold all these?

1883
01:39:41,840 --> 01:39:42,924
Yeah. Come here.

1884
01:39:42,924 --> 01:39:45,301
They're checks.
They're from my dad's friends.

1885
01:39:45,301 --> 01:39:47,554
They're for us, so we can
start a new life... Hey!

1886
01:39:47,554 --> 01:39:49,180
What are you doing?
What's wrong?

1887
01:39:49,180 --> 01:39:50,932
We have to leave.

1888
01:39:50,932 --> 01:39:52,809
What?!

1889
01:39:52,809 --> 01:39:55,812
Brenda, you love me, right?

1890
01:39:55,812 --> 01:39:56,813
Yes.

1891
01:39:56,813 --> 01:39:57,939
I mean, you'd love me
no matter what.

1892
01:39:57,939 --> 01:39:58,940
Yes.

1893
01:39:58,940 --> 01:39:59,941
I mean, you'd love me

1894
01:39:59,941 --> 01:40:01,526
whether I was sick
or whether I was poor

1895
01:40:01,526 --> 01:40:02,902
or even if I had
a different name.

1896
