for the rest of our lives

1922
01:40:52,702 --> 01:40:54,162
- Look.

1923
01:40:54,162 --> 01:40:56,873
Frank, stop teasing me.

1924
01:40:56,873 --> 01:40:58,166
You're Frank Conners.

1925
01:40:58,166 --> 01:41:01,252
You're Frank Conners,
and you're 2: years old and...

1926
01:41:01,252 --> 01:41:02,588
Brenda...

1927
01:41:02,588 --> 01:41:04,672
Why would you lie to me?

1928
01:41:04,672 --> 01:41:06,925
- Brenda, Brenda...
- I want to know your name.

1929
01:41:06,925 --> 01:41:09,010
- Listen to me, Brenda.
- Tell me your name.

1930
01:41:09,010 --> 01:41:10,428
We can live anywhere we want

1931
01:41:10,428 --> 01:41:12,013
but you have to trust me,
Brenda.

1932
01:41:12,013 --> 01:41:13,389
- Do you trust me?
- Yes.

1933
01:41:13,389 --> 01:41:15,433
- Do you love me, Brenda?
- Yes.

1934
01:41:15,433 --> 01:41:16,893
- You love me?
- I love you.

1935
01:41:16,893 --> 01:41:19,437
Excuse me, Mother.

1936
01:41:19,437 --> 01:41:21,856
Honey, this is Mr. Hanratty.
My wife Carol.

1937
01:41:21,856 --> 01:41:23,942
- Oh, Mister...?
- Hanratty, ma'am.

1938
01:41:23,942 --> 01:41:24,984
- Ratty.
- Yes.

1939
01:41:24,984 --> 01:41:26,445
Have you seen Frank or Brenda?

1940
01:41:26,445 --> 01:41:28,571
I-I think they went upstairs.

1941
01:41:34,077 --> 01:41:35,745
Frank...

1942
01:41:37,455 --> 01:41:39,415
:
Brenda, come here.

1943
01:41:39,415 --> 01:41:41,459
Okay, in two days,
you're going to meet me

1944
01:41:41,459 --> 01:41:43,628
